Integrate long-term physical, chemical, ecological, and working consequences (@mine-closure-project: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @mining-and-mineral-engineering, #source "../sources/Preventing-Acid-and-Metalliferous-Drainage.lingua#r_7SDBPF4TAZV9GKDCTW9BTYJ43R", #source "../sources/Mine-Water-Stewardship-Handbook.lingua#r_4Y8Q03RFJBVBN6WVVY3EN6Q5DM", #source "../sources/Tailings-Management-Leading-Practice.lingua#r_40NN1207ZCBP7RVX690CP4G7HZ", #source "../sources/Mine-Closure-Leading-Practice.lingua#r_2GYS4C9MHF2CRD8253QPDEV3QN", #source "../sources/Mine-Rehabilitation-Leading-Practice.lingua#r_4RS2D5ZYYW6Q7EG62C4VDWGWYQ", #source "../sources/Global-Industry-Standard-on-Tailings-Management.lingua#r_2S0TS7YDGRXD4EFA14DWNQ351S", #source "../sources/Community-Engagement-and-Development-Handbook.lingua#r_2RSVNSY8QJJ3XF6YGJ7TBADM89", #mining-and-mineral-engineering "Integrated-mine-to-product-design-operation-and-recovery.lingua#r_1WXCC9JS4RM4E27NGJC8ZXYE5B") { r_6GENN45MN7EKVN1GRKXQPYH1K0
**Read:** [Preventing acid and metalliferous drainage — leading-practice handbook](../sources/Preventing-Acid-and-Metalliferous-Drainage.lingua#r_7SDBPF4TAZV9GKDCTW9BTYJ43R), the whole handbook; [Water stewardship — Australian leading-practice handbook](../sources/Mine-Water-Stewardship-Handbook.lingua#r_4Y8Q03RFJBVBN6WVVY3EN6Q5DM), the whole handbook; [Tailings management — Australian leading-practice handbook](../sources/Tailings-Management-Leading-Practice.lingua#r_40NN1207ZCBP7RVX690CP4G7HZ), the whole handbook; [Mine closure — Australian leading-practice handbook](../sources/Mine-Closure-Leading-Practice.lingua#r_2GYS4C9MHF2CRD8253QPDEV3QN), the whole handbook; [Mine rehabilitation — Australian leading-practice handbook](../sources/Mine-Rehabilitation-Leading-Practice.lingua#r_4RS2D5ZYYW6Q7EG62C4VDWGWYQ), the whole handbook; [Global Industry Standard on Tailings Management — Global Tailings Review](../sources/Global-Industry-Standard-on-Tailings-Management.lingua#r_2S0TS7YDGRXD4EFA14DWNQ351S), the full standard; [Community engagement and development — Australian leading-practice handbook](../sources/Community-Engagement-and-Development-Handbook.lingua#r_2RSVNSY8QJJ3XF6YGJ7TBADM89), the whole handbook and chosen case evidence.

Choose a public mine/plant lifecycle case with sufficient material, water, ground, environmental, and historical evidence. Read the complete drainage, water, tailings, closure, and rehabilitation handbooks and full GISTM. Read the original technical studies underlying the particular geochemical, hydraulic, geotechnical, ecological, and monitoring claims actually used.

Construct compatible material domains, geometries, water balances, exposure histories, and time horizons across the models. Explain what is observed, calibrated, projected, or assumed and where the models exchange quantities. A geochemical prediction using one water history and a stability model using an incompatible pore-pressure history do not form an integrated design.

Compare two substantive waste/storage/closure arrangements, including normal and early closure, changed climate/water boundaries, incomplete construction, and continuing maintenance. Evaluate technical performance, consequences to affected people, uncertainty, monitoring, response, and the resources and knowledge needed after production ends. Distinguish a handbook/voluntary-standard interpretation from a claim about actual legal acceptance.

**Work:** independently reproduce one central prediction and validate against later or withheld observations. Trace at least one consequential discrepancy across model boundaries and defend an alternative explanation. Produce a closure work/monitoring account, explicit outcome criteria, and an evidence-based revision. Identify what remains unresolved and how another team could preserve the observations, interpret a change, and perform the continuing work. A visually improved site is not the sole evidence of long-term success.

**Continue:** [Build a coherent mine-to-product study across extraction, processing, operation, and closure](Integrated-mine-to-product-design-operation-and-recovery.lingua#r_1WXCC9JS4RM4E27NGJC8ZXYE5B).

**Return:** [Mining and mineral engineering — extraction, processing, and continuing work](../Mining-and-mineral-engineering.lingua#r_22HJPS3RTK5EX1J55YJP75PHYA).
